- 9,133) / 9,133 = 7.62% [10Q.IS.4].\\n- GAAP operating margin: 1,942 / 9,829 = 19.76%; prior year 1,709 / 9,133 = 18.71%. Expansion = +104.5 bps. Computed from dollar rows, not by subtracting the rounded 19.8% and 18.7% disclosures.\\n- Non-GAAP operating margin: 3,172 / 9,829 = 32.27%; prior year 2,928 / 9,133 = 32.05%. Expansion = +21.2 bps.\\n- GAAP margin expansion (+104.5 bps) is roughly 5x the non-GAAP expansion (+21.2 bps). The assertion that non-GAAP margin improvement 'confirms equally strong operating leverage' is not supported; GAAP leverage was substantially stronger.\\n\\n2. NON-GAAP ADDBACKS\\n- Total addbacks: 395 (purchased-intangible amortization) + 799 (SBC) + 36 (restructuring) = 1,230. Reconciliation check: 1,942 + 1,230 = 3,172, matching reported non-GAAP operating income [EX99.NONGAAP.OP].\\n- The 799 SBC addback already excludes the 15 of SBC embedded in the 36 restructuring addback (10-Q total SBC was 814 = 799 + 15). No double-counting.\\n- Addbacks as % of GAAP operating income: 1,230 / 1,942 = 63.3%. Non-GAAP operating income is 1.64x GAAP.\\n- Exhibit 99.1 explicitly labels non-GAAP measures as supplemental, not GAAP substitutes, and warns methods may differ among companies.\\n\\n3. FREE CASH FLOW\\n- Q1 FY2026 FCF: 6,476 - 179 = 6,297. Q1 FY2025 FCF: 6,247 - 163 = 6,084. Growth = 3.5% [10Q.CF.7, EX99.NONGAAP.FCF].\\n- FY2025 FCF: 13,092 - 658 = 12,434. FY2024 FCF: 10,234 - 736 = 9,498. Growth = 30.9% [10K.CF.63].\\n- Mechanical annualization of Q1 FCF: 6,297 x 4 = 25,188. This is a mechanical extrapolation, not a forecast.\\n\\n4. CASH-CONVERSION QUALITY\\n- Q1 CFO / net income: 6,476 / 1,541 = 4.20x. FY2025: 13,092 / 6,197 = 2.11x. FY2024: 10,234 / 4,136 = 2.47x [10K.IS.60, 10K.CF.63, 10Q.IS.4, 10Q.CF.7].\\n- The Q1 ratio is elevated vs. full-year norms. The six disclosed operating-asset/liability changes sum to +2,670 (AR +7,591; capitalized contract costs -365; prepaid/other -481; AP/accrued/other -1,007; operating lease liabilities 