591) and other working-capital items. This is seasonality/timing, not a structural improvement in earnings quality.\\n  (c) Non-GAAP margin expansion (+21 bps) was far smaller than GAAP margin expansion (+105 bps). The assertion that non-GAAP 'confirms equally strong operating leverage' is contradicted by the data; GAAP leverage was much stronger.\\n  (d) Non-GAAP measures are explicitly labeled supplemental, not GAAP substitutes [EX99.NONGAAP.OP].\\n- Cash quality assessment: mixed_seasonality_distorted. FCF grew modestly (+3.5% YoY), but the elevated CFO/NI conversion is driven by working-capital timing, not a clean structural improvement.\\n\\n8. LIMITATIONS\\n- Interim unaudited data: Q1 statements are unaudited three-month interim statements [PERIOD.10Q.2].\\n- Seasonality: Q1 cash flows and margins are not necessarily representative of the full fiscal year.\\n- Non-GAAP comparability: Methods may differ among companies; non-GAAP is supplemental [EX99.NONGAAP.OP].\\n- No forecast: Mechanical annualization is not a forecast.\\n- No investment recommendation: This memo is analytical only; no buy/sell/hold recommendation is made.\"\n}\n</FINAL_JSON>",
